1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,484
Thenar sells robot demonstration data, and its own

2
00:00:06,514 --> 00:00:08,603
server is the party being checked.

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:12,154
So a Chainlink CRE workflow audits it.

4
00:00:12,834 --> 00:00:16,960
This is the CRE CLI running the corpus-audit workflow.

5
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:20,745
On a cron trigger, every node fetches the served episode

6
00:00:20,775 --> 00:00:24,832
hashes over HTTP and rebuilds each task's Merkle root

7
00:00:24,862 --> 00:00:28,279
itself, with consensus on identical roots.

8
00:00:28,459 --> 00:00:31,749
Then it reads the roots our verifier committed on Monad,

9
00:00:31,779 --> 00:00:35,592
in one Multicall3 call, decides a verdict per task, and

10
00:00:35,622 --> 00:00:38,448
writes a report to the CorpusAudit contract on Monad

11
00:00:38,478 --> 00:00:44,415
testnet. Here it audited three tasks, in transaction 0xf154.

12
00:00:45,095 --> 00:00:47,160
The app reads the verdict back.

13
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:49,327
For this task it is uncommitted:

14
00:00:49,357 --> 00:00:52,630
the episodes are served, but no root is committed yet,

15
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:57,940
and CRE says so on chain, beside the data, for any buyer to read.

16
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,362
Chainlink CRE, auditing the data Thenar sells, on Monad.

